   "scholar": "Lfmhbd8AAAAJ",
   "bio": "Robert Gilmore Pontius Jr is Professor in the Graduate School of Geography at Clark University, where he has taught since 1998. He holds a PhD in Environmental Science from the State University of New York College of Environmental Science and Forestry and a Master of Applied Statistics from The Ohio State University. He creates quantitative methods for GIScience, remote sensing, and statistics, among them quantity and allocation disagreement, Intensity Analysis, and the Total Operating Characteristic, and several of these methods are built into the TerrSet software, formerly IDRISI. He was a Fulbright Scholar in Brazil in 2022 to 2023. His book <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-030-70765-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Metrics That Make a Difference: How to Analyze Change and Error</a> (Springer, 2022) brings these methods together for students and researchers.",
